<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111617" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλόψῡχ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>loving one's life,</i>
			with collat. sense of <i>cowardly, faint-hearted,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					348
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				10.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δειλὸν δ᾽ ὁ πλοῦτος καὶ φ. κακόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					597
				</span></i>
			 (troch.). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-χως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					3.137
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chor.
					35.139
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				p.429
			</span></i> F.-R. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>loving men's lives</i> or <i>souls,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέσποτα φιλόψυχε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Wi.</u>
					11.26
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
